{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T082349Z_dev-01_flat_fed5", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "For the SFDM benchmark (m_ψ = 47.75 GeV, m_h2 = 14.325 GeV, r = 0.3), the paper gives these h2 branching fractions: Br(h2→b b̄) = 0.7910, Br(h2→c c̄) = 0.1281 and Br(h2→τ⁺τ⁻) = 0.0797. The 4b final state accounts for approximately 62.6% of h2h2 decays. This matches 0.7910² ≈ 0.626.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "7.2"}]}, "turns": 2, "seconds": 3.961, "tool_calls": 1, "tool_result_chars": 147086, "input_tokens": 6, "output_tokens": 277, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 67399, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:23:54+00:00"}
